WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.440
Writer-director James Gunn has described his
easter egg obsession as "insane".

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.670
And for Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2, Gunn
has said that he worked extra hard to sneak

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.780
even more weird and wonderful easter eggs
into the movie than he did in the first one.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.780
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and, if you've seen Guardians Vol. 2 now,

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:21.939
you'll know there are plenty of easter eggs,
MCU references and in-jokes that even casual

00:00:21.939 --> 00:00:23.189
viewers will have noticed.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:26.820
But, in this video I want to take a look at
10 of the coolest easter eggs that you might

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.260
have missed or which only hard-core fans will
have spotted.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.400
If you want to let me know about any others
you saw or particularly enjoyed, just leave

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.540
a comment below and make sure you're also
subscribed to be entered into my awesome Guardians

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.190
of the Galaxy giveaway.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:43.370
Of course, spoilers lie ahead for Guardians
of the Galaxy Vol. 2, so if you haven't seen

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:47.330
the movie yet, you can tap in the top-right
of the screen for my spoiler-free review and

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.299
come back here after you've seen the movie.

00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:54.830
During one of the jump gate scenes when Yondu,
Rocket and Groot are travelling to Ego's planet,

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:58.900
you no doubt spotted Stan Lee's brilliant
cameo with a group of Watchers, but, there's

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.110
a blink-and-you'll-miss-it moment during an
earlier sequence when Yondu's ship streaked

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:06.530
past a rocky planet where two aliens seem
to be duking it out.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:11.170
You'll need to watch the scene very carefully
to spot that the aliens are a pair of Kronans.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:16.430
We last saw a Kronan as part of the Marauders
who attacked Vanaheim in Thor: The Dark World.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:20.390
Thor defeated the Kronan easily with his hammer
in that movie, but we're definitely seeing

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:25.050
more Kronans soon in the MCU as Thor: Ragnarok
director Taika Waititi revealed that he'll

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:28.310
be playing the part of Korg in the third Thor
movie.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:32.300
In the comics, the Kronan stone man Korg was
enslaved together with the Hulk on the planet

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.300
Sakaar.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:37.250
By the way, there's another cool Thor: Ragnarok
tease in the movie which I'll reveal later.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:42.621
Vol. 2 delves deeper into Nebula and Gamora's
backstory and the abuse they suffered at the

00:01:42.621 --> 00:01:44.960
hands of their adoptive father Thanos.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.131
In the scene after Nebula and Gamora fight,
Nebula gives and horrific explanation of how

00:01:49.131 --> 00:01:54.460
Thanos punished her every time she lost when
he set her and Gamora against each other,

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:58.770
for example, he pulled her eye from her head,
her brain from her skull, and her arm from

00:01:58.770 --> 00:01:59.770
her body.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:04.060
As well as being a devastating part of Nebula's
backstory in the movie, this is actually also

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.990
an easter egg to a moment in the Infinity
Gauntlet storyline in the comics where Thanos

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:12.250
tortures Nebula after he discovers that she
pretended to be his granddaughter.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:17.270
As punishment, Thanos wreaks havoc on Nebula's
body before presenting her to Mistress Death,

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.500
who he wishes to impress.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.230
Sylvester Stallone makes a small but important
appearance in Vol. 2, setting himself up in

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:28.440
a mid-credits scene as the leader of a new
team of Ravagers who we'll probably see in

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:29.550
the next Guardians movie.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:34.830
The team he's forming is a nod to the original
Guardians of the Galaxy team in the comics,

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:39.349
and I've got an in-depth video on Stakar's
new team which I'll link to in the video description.

00:02:39.349 --> 00:02:43.590
But what you might have missed earlier in
the movie was a neat easter egg to Stakar's

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.410
comic book origins.

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:49.540
During the scene on the planet Contraxia,
when Stakar is arguing with Yondu about exiling

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:53.580
him from the Ravager clan for breaking their
code by trafficking children, he tells Yondu

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:57.120
that "the colours of Ogord will not flash
over your grave."

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.380
Ogord is Stakar's surname which he was given
in the comics after he was adopted as a baby

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.560
by a Reaver leader called Ogord [who also
raised Stakar with another adopted child,

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:04.560
his sister Aleta].

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.161
Stakar's words, of course, also foreshadow
Yondu's sad but heroic death at the end of

00:03:08.161 --> 00:03:12.470
the movie, after which the Ravagers return
to honour their fallen comrade, releasing

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.660
the colours of Ogord during Yondu's funeral.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:20.530
In the scene where Ego is teaching Peter Quill
about his Celestial powers, Ego taps Peter

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:24.630
in the middle of his forehead, which reminded
me of the Ancient One, Doctor Strange and

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:27.740
the idea of the Third Eye in the MCU's last
film.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:32.220
But the point I want to focus on here is that
we see Peter's eyes fill with black.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:36.350
Then little lights and what look like planets
and stars appear in his eyes as well.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:40.560
As this happens, Peter whispers the words
"I can see it … eternity."

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:46.160
This scene is a nod to the comic book character
Eternity whose body has a kind of galaxy-style

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:50.230
silhouette and who also has black eyes with
a star in the middle.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:54.960
Interestingly, in the comics, Eternity appears
in multiple stories with Doctor Strange, as

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:59.459
well as the Infinity War, Infinity Gauntlet,
and Infinity Watch storylines.

00:03:59.459 --> 00:04:04.030
Talking of eyes, there's a great call-back
to a joke from the first Guardians movie in

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:08.069
the scene where Yondu and Rocket are locked
up after the Ravager mutiny.

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:12.879
Yondu asks baby Groot to get his prototype
fin from the Captain's quarters, but Groot

00:04:12.879 --> 00:04:17.910
brings back a variety of weird items including
Yondu's underpants, a squealing Orloni creature,

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:19.370
and a mechanical eye.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:23.530
In the first film, as the Guardians prepared
to face off against Ronan, Rocket pretended

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:27.099
he needed one of the Ravager's mechanical
eyes to complete the plan.

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:31.900
Star-Lord realised Rocket was goofing around
and refused him, but in this scene in Vol.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:36.031
2, Rocket finally got his wish and found it
hilarious that the Ravager was going to be

00:04:36.031 --> 00:04:38.040
missing his eye when he woke up.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.960
By the way, when Yondu eventually got his
new fin, it was a nice nod to the much taller

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:46.009
Mohawk fin that Yondu's character has in the
comics.

00:04:46.009 --> 00:04:50.350
Star-Lord's new T-shirt design for Vol. 2
is written in an alien language that first

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:54.289
appeared on a keyboard display during the
Kyln prison sequence in the first Guardians

00:04:54.289 --> 00:04:55.289
movie.

00:04:55.289 --> 00:04:59.280
The letters spell out "Gears Shift", which
according to Chris Pratt, is the brand name

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.909
of a space candy.

00:05:00.909 --> 00:05:04.900
And just below the main logo on the T-shirt
are some really small words that translate

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.270
as "A TENEYCK GALAXY INVENTION".

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:11.270
Karen TenEyck is actually the designer who
worked on these costume graphics for Guardians

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:16.940
of the Galaxy Vol. 2, and her previous credits
include Captain America: The First Avenger.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:20.900
The original song "Guardians Inferno" that
plays at the end of the movie is credited

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:23.180
to "The Sneepers featuring David Hasselhoff".

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:27.889
Hasselhoff, of course, was referenced multiple
times in the movie and appeared briefly when

00:05:27.889 --> 00:05:29.180
Ego took on his appearance.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:33.719
However, the name "Sneepers" is actually an
easter egg to an aggressive race of aliens

00:05:33.719 --> 00:05:40.889
who invaded numerous planets and first appeared
in #49 of the comic Tales of Suspense in 1964.

00:05:40.889 --> 00:05:45.181
In that comic, Uatu the Watcher used them
as a cautionary tale and warned that the alien

00:05:45.181 --> 00:05:50.330
race were watching Earth and waiting for mankind
to destroy itself with nuclear weapons.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:54.820
By the way, the owner of the Iron Lotus, the
bar that Yondu and the Ravagers visit on Contraxia,

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:55.820
is a Sneeper.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:06:01.059
The creature trying to steal the Sovereign's
Batteries is called an Abilisk, a beast that's

00:06:01.059 --> 00:06:04.099
new to the Marvel Cinematic Universe in Vol.
2.

00:06:04.099 --> 00:06:07.969
But the look of the Abilisk seems to take
inspiration from the creatures in the comics

00:06:07.969 --> 00:06:10.089
called The Many-Angled Ones.

00:06:10.089 --> 00:06:14.610
The Many-Angled Ones are linked with the Cancerverse,
and like the Abilisk, they often manifest

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:18.839
themselves as sharp-toothed monstrosities
with masses of tentacles.

00:06:18.839 --> 00:06:21.819
Given the appearance of the creature in this
movie, it'll be interesting to see if the

00:06:21.819 --> 00:06:26.030
Cancerverse will inspire new creatures and
storylines for Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.030
3.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:31.729
You'll have to pay really close attention,
but there's a brief cameo by actor Gregg Henry

00:06:31.729 --> 00:06:34.849
who played Grandpa Quill in the first Guardians
movie.

00:06:34.849 --> 00:06:38.930
In a scene on Earth, he's driving a car with
his friend, and gets pushed along by the huge

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:43.220
blue blob that multiplies after Ego activates
his seedlings to take over the galaxy.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:47.770
By the way, also cameo'ing earlier in the
scene are James Gunn's parents, who are the

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:51.970
older couple who ask what the blob is as they
film it on their phones.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:56.110
The end credits also have a little cameo by
Grandpa Quill who appears in a little bubble

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:57.199
as the credits roll.

00:06:57.199 --> 00:07:01.520
There's also a small cameo by Jeff Goldblum
dancing in another bubble during the credits,

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:04.860
a tease to his appearance as Grandmaster in
Thor: Ragnarok.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:08.649
Plus there are cameos by characters who appeared
in the credits of the first Guardians of the

00:07:08.649 --> 00:07:13.409
Galaxy movie like Cosmo the Spacedog and Howard
the Duck, who also appears briefly in this

00:07:13.409 --> 00:07:15.419
movie during the scene on Contraxia.

00:07:15.419 --> 00:07:19.449
Also, watch the credits even more carefully
and you'll notice that some of the cast and

00:07:19.449 --> 00:07:23.050
crew names are replaced for a few seconds
with the words "I AM GROOT".

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:27.180
